  "subject": "a neighbourhood chief who forgets to switch off the loudspeaker while his wife finds his secret stash",
  "caption": "Taiwanese Hokkien liam-kua, the traditional street-corner narrative song. A gekkin moon lute plucking a bright, loose pentatonic accompaniment with short fills between lines, and a daguangxian large bowed fiddle with a coconut-shell body shadowing the voice in heterophony, and nothing else. A loose pulse that stretches at the end of each four-line stanza. Dry, close and intimate, like two players on stools at a temple-front corner, the voice forward with the two instruments on either side. An older female storyteller, half-sung and half-spoken, in rhymed four-line seven-syllable stanzas, with spoken asides delivered in dry deadpan humour. 76 BPM, D pentatonic. Gossipy, deadpan and delighted. No drums, no opera gongs or cymbals, no gezaixi falsetto, no Chinese orchestra, no guitar, no synth, no jazz harmony, no rap, no enka-style weeping.",
  "lyrics": "[Verse]\n月琴彈起予恁聽\n阮庄里長上蓋拚\n送一桶瓦斯嘛講\n早起六點就出聲\n\n[Chorus]\n放送頭仔咧放送\n規庄的耳空攏咧聽\n\n[Verse]\n報告煞了真歡喜\n開關猶開無注意\n伊的牽手行入來\n一句一句放出去\n\n[Verse]\n「你莫假仙 我攏知影矣」\n\n[Verse]\n你的私奇藏佗位\n放送頭跤彼个櫃\n三萬八千報紙捲\n規庄聽甲笑歪喙\n\n[Chorus]\n放送頭仔咧放送\n三萬八 這馬是伊某的\n\n[Outro]\n隔轉工 早起六點\n「報告里民 昨昏的代誌 莫閣講矣」",
